["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 397, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 2, "prompt": "\nYou hear a nurse briefing her colleague about a patient.\nWhat does she want her colleague to do?\nA. Check the patient is receiving the correct amount of fluids.\nB. Order another chest radiograph to check for an effusion.\nC. Confirm the patient is stable and check his blood culture.", "sourcePage": 1, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 723, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "\nYou hear part of a consultation at a GP practice with a patient suffering from depression\nand sleep disturbances.\nThe GP recommends cognitive behavioural therapy because\nA. there are better ways for the patient to respond to life's challenges.\nB. it will help the patient better manage the way he feels when stressed.\nC. the patient needs to control his anger and medication isn't working.", "sourcePage": 2, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "\nYou hear a nurse seeking advice from a doctor.\nWhy does the nurse telephone the doctor?\nA. She would like to know how to proceed with the patient.\nB. The patient is in intense pain and has a fever.\nC. She suspects that the patient has an infection.", "sourcePage": 2, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 483, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "\nYou hear the principal of an aged care home talking to staff about osteoporosis.\nShe wants to highlight that\nA. there are now treatments available for men.\nB. residents are not getting enough calcium and vitamin D.\nC. a lot of the residents may already have osteoporosis.", "sourcePage": 2, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 831, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "\nYou hear two nurses discussing a patient, Mrs Robbins.\nJulie says Mrs Robbins refused to mobilise because\nA. she was happy having a sponge bath.\nB. she wanted to hear directly from the doctor.\nC. she was upset and wanted to be left alone.\nOur Brochures\nVirtual Class Brochure\nGroup Classes Brochure\nHome\n Privacy Policy\n Terms of Use\n   Technology Requirements\n Articles\nSocial networks", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 19, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["abcb1720f89b4f0bdfd9cce5dea4a744e5c17e96079c55b6c167420659845abc"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-53002d2b0e211ea123b9", "filename": "Listening Part B-answers.docx", "sha256": "53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.docx", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/53002d2b0e211ea123b91537c38f560493149ae05c9f519112fdd0f45941c155.json", "format": "docx", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}]}
